{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>The blessings of your father.</b> And may He also bless you with the blessings of your father — they are as it says: וּפָרַצְתָּ יָמָּה וָקֵדְמָה וְצָפוֹנָה וָנֶגְבָּה (Genesis 28:14), which is inheritance without bounds, and as it says: וְנִבְרְכוּ בְךָ כָּל מִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲדָמָה וּבְזַרְעֶךָ (Genesis 12:3). This is what is destined for the survivors whom YHWH calls, as it says: כָּעֵת יֵאָמֵר לְיַעֲקֹב וּלְיִשְׂרָאֵל מַה פָּעַל אֵל (Numbers 23:23), and as it says: וְאַתֶּם כֹּהֲנֵי ה' תִּקָּרֵאוּ (Isaiah 61:6), and as it says: יַחֲזִיקוּ עֲשָׂרָה אֲנָשִׁים מִכָּל לְשֹׁנוֹת הַגּוֹיִם וְהֶחֱזִיקוּ בִּכְנַף אִישׁ יְהוּדִי לֵאמֹר נֵלְכָה עִמָּכֶם כִּי שָׁמַעְנוּ אֱלֹהִים עִמָּכֶם (Zechariah 8:23)." "<b>They prevail over the blessings of my parents.</b> And I said <b>the blessings of your father</b> because they prevail over the blessings that my parents received." "<b>Unto the desire of the everlasting hills.</b> That my blessings extended to the boundary of the two sides of the sphere of the sun's course, from the center, which bound the dry land — they are the two extremities of the temporal and perishable world. And he called them גִּבְעוֹת עוֹלָם, the everlasting hills, after its two parts that bound the dry land, because of their height above the earth's center, in the image of a hill. And these blessings of his were when it was said to him: וּפָרַצְתָּ וְנִבְרְכוּ בְךָ, which is the blessing of eternal felitude, through which the entire human species is blessed." "<b>They shall be on the head of Joseph.</b> From the mouth of the Most High, Who sends His blessings from on high upon the head of Joseph without intermediary. And so Moses our Master said, after saying וּרְצוֹן שֹׁכְנִי סְנֶה (Deuteronomy 33:16) — which refers to the El of the heights, Whose blessings are from on high — תְּבוֹאתָה לְרֹאשׁ יוֹסֵף." "<b>And on the crown of the head of him who was separated from his brothers.</b> This is because when he was a nazirite, crowned with the nezer, ruling among his brothers, his deeds testified that he is worthy to receive blessings from El blessed be He without intermediary. And so his seed was of a rank close to the tribe of kingship, as it says (Hosea 13:1): כִּדְבַר אֶפְרַיִם רְתֵת נָשִׂיא הוּא בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל, and from him was the first of the judges, and the first king was chosen when the kingship of the house of David was divided."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:38.364464911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}